/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A flash drum does in one step what a column does in many.
   - F is feed flow (kmol/h), z its mole fraction, V and L vapour and liquid flows (kmol/h), and y and x their mole fractions.
   - F feed flow (kmol/h); z feed mole fraction; V, L vapour and liquid flows (kmol/h); y, x their mole fractions.
   - At equilibrium yi = Ki xi.
   - Degrees of freedom decide the drum.
   - The unknown is usually V/F.
   - sum over every component i; zi feed mole fraction; Ki K value at drum T and P; V/F vapour fraction, the unknown.
   - The left side falls steadily as ψ rises, so when two phases exist there is a single root with 0 < ψ < 1; at the bubble point the root is ψ = 0 and at the dew point ψ = 1.
   - zA, zB are feed mole fractions summing to 1; KA, KB are the two K values at the drum T and P.
   - Test for two phases first.
*/
