/* book: lead: Simple distillation is the oldest batch separation: heat a liquid charge, remove the vapour as it forms, and condense it. Because the vapour is richer in the more volatile component, the pot liquid changes during the run. A differential balance gives the Rayleigh equation, which connects the starting and ending liquid amounts and compositions. Steam distillation uses a second immiscible liquid, us */
